#
# Trivy vulnerability exclusions. Each entry states why the finding
# does not apply here. Anything without a justification does not
# belong in this file.

# GO-2026-5932: golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained and unsafe
# by design. The advisory has no fixed version and never will, because
# the remedy is to stop using that package rather than to upgrade it.
#
# This repository never imports golang.org/x/crypto; the module is a
# transitive dependency only. The OpenPGP work goes through
# github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp (internal/adapters/openpgp),
# which is the maintained fork the advisory itself points at.
# govulncheck agrees: it reports no reachable path, and it gates the
# same PRs this file does.
#
# Revisit if the main module ever imports golang.org/x/crypto directly.
GO-2026-5932
